'''Resort De La Cospa''' (行楽地デラ・コスパ ''Kōrakuchi Dera・Kosupa'', '''Tourist Resort Dela Cospa''') is the 14th sub-chapter of [[Zero Legends]], and the 112th sub-chapter overall. It was introduced in [[Version 13.6 Update|Version 13.6]] and is available up to {{2c}} difficulty.

==Difficulty==
This sub-chapter is overall easier than the previous ones, featuring mostly straightforward stages with very few true threats. The only significantly difficult stage here is [[Private Beach]], which focuses heavily on Metal enemies supported by a [[Dark Dober]]. Due to the constant Knockback and push pressure, this stage relies heavily on [[critical]] hits; without consistent crit RNG, [[Dark Dober]] will quickly shred through your frontline.

The rest of the sub-chapter frequently focuses on [[Diabrollow]] and the Knockback ability for many stages, but they generally do not form overwhelming combinations. As a result, most of the sub-chapter can be cleared comfortably with standard [[Sage Slayer]] or high-range options.

The sub-chapter culminates in [[Costly Emigration]], featuring a 150% [[Perfect Cyclone]] backed by heavy push support, acting almost like a condensed throwback to [[Red Sky at Morning]]. While not extremely difficult, careless play here can result in rapid frontline collapse due to constant KB pressure.
{{LegendDiff|120}}

==New Features==
This sub-chapter introduces 2 enemies to Zero Legends:
*[[Diabrollow]]: An [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]/[[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] variant of [[Brollow]] with guaranteed level 3 [[Mini-Wave]]s and Knockback.
*[[The Perfect Cyclone]]: A [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] [[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]] from [[Red Sky at Morning]]. Has incredibly long range for a Cyclone (650), but deals relatively low damage per hit and cannot hit units within 249 range.

